id: pm-gh1538
title: "GH-1538: refuse or honor supplied MCP update fields before reporting success"
description: "Reported against published2026.10.21: pm_update with priority/status beside options:{} returns changed_field_count:0 and warnings while nested options mutate correctly. Source report https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1538 provides a sandboxed stdio reproduction and costs. Existing closed warning-only work deliberately preserves success; this report requests a stronger mutation-outcome contract. Current code still contains warning-only unexpected-option handling. Fresh public protocol and persistence reproduction is required before choosing flat-field support or pre-dispatch refusal."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[3]: agent-ux,github-report,sdk
created_at: "2026-10-21T21:28:02.196Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-22T01:31:07.844Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-22T01:06:43.106Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-22T01:06:43.106Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 120
acceptance_criteria: Prove advertised schema-to-dispatch persistence through the public MCP entrypoint; Honor supported supplied mutation fields or refuse with precise nesting recovery before execution; Preserve documented precedence and extension passthrough compatibility; Demonstrate unchanged tracker bytes/history on refusal
parent: pm-5k4v
risk: medium
confidence: 80
severity: medium
resolution: "MCP create/update dispatch uses canonical SDK mutation contracts, nested alias precedence and typed no-loss preflight; valid project-defined fields retain their native lookup semantics."
expected_result: "Advertised MCP update fields persist or refuse atomically; nested options win, custom fields work and native SDK update admission stays strict."
actual_result: "Modern discovered flat priority/status persist with changed_field_count 2; nested precedence, tags, estimate, comments, file links and literal body pass. Malformed scalar/list/container/force requests refuse before changes and preserve exact item/history bytes. Full coverage and packed consumers pass."
